sequenceDiagram
    participant A as A (sender)
    participant B as B (receiver)
    Note over A: sendfile clearml.conf — 14162 B
    Note over A,B: DEFLATE the file WHOLE, then split.<br/>14162 B → 5015 B on air (2.82x). Compressing each<br/>3 kB part separately would throw the ratio away
    Note over A,B: peer not heard from recently — ctl_tx_rung decays<br/>one rung per 90 s, so committing now would open at a<br/>rung the link was never tested at (measured, 37.0 s<br/>at rung 4 where the next exchange settled at rung 12)
    A->>B: LINK probe (QoS control, sub-second)
    B->>A: ACK  req_rung, snr_report
    Note over A: ladder refreshed — only NOW is the transfer committed
    Note over A,B: part 1 of 2 — a selective-repeat window in ONE transmission
    A->>B: preamble + header + frag 0 (ack_req set)
    A->>B: frag 1, frag 2, ... (streamed, ZC resync every 4 blocks)
    A->>B: frag N (ack_req set)
    Note over A,B: ack_req rides the FIRST block as well as the last,<br/>so a peer that cannot follow the stream still replies<br/>and the sender falls back by bitmap, not by timeout
    B->>A: ACK + bitmap of missing fragments
    A->>B: retransmit only the missing fragments
    B->>A: ACK — window complete
    Note over A,B: part 2 of 2 — same window mechanics
    A->>B: streamed window
    B->>A: ACK + bitmap
    Note over A,B: parts arrive in order (FIFO bulk queue),<br/>then inflate the whole DEFLATE stream once
    Note over B: stored as rx_clearml.conf — 14162 B, 2 parts,<br/>5015 B on air = 2.82x compression
